+# Requirements → Test Matrix
+
+**Feature**: `001-bookmark-manager-cli` | **Date**: 2026-11-20
+
+Constitution Principle III requires every functional requirement to map to at least one
+automated `pytest` test; Principle V requires every security requirement to map to at least
+one test **including a negative case**. SC-002 requires 100% coverage of FR-001…FR-027 and
+SR-001…SR-011 plus every acceptance scenario in User Stories 1–4.
+
+This matrix is the artifact the Test gate and the Review gate are audited against. The named
+test functions are the planned contract; `/speckit-tasks` turns each row into work.
+
+**Coverage**: 27 FR + 11 SR = **38 requirements, 38 mapped, 0 unmapped, 0 planned skips.**
+(`test_file_mode_is_0600` carries a POSIX-only guard — on Windows it is skipped and SR-005 is
+unverifiable there by construction; on the project's stated target platform it always runs.)
+
+## Functional requirements
+
+| Req | Test file | Test function | Assertion |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| FR-001 | contract/test_cli_surface.py | `test_five_subcommands_exist` / `test_module_is_runnable` | each of `add`/`list`/`search`/`delete`/`export` parses; `bookmarks.__main__` imports and exposes the entry call |
+| FR-002 | integration/test_story1_add_and_list.py | `test_db_option_is_used` / `test_default_db_is_cwd_bookmarks_db` | `--db` path holds the data; with no `--db`, `bookmarks.db` appears in the cwd |
+| FR-003 | integration/test_persistence.py | `test_missing_file_is_created_with_schema` / `test_existing_file_is_reused` | first use creates file + schema; second invocation sees prior rows |
+| FR-004 | contract/test_exit_statuses.py | `test_every_successful_command_exits_zero` | all five commands return 0 on valid input |
+| FR-005 | contract/test_exit_statuses.py | `test_error_status_and_stream_mapping` | parametrised over every documented failure: message on stderr, stdout clean, status ∈ {1,2,3} as tabled |
+| FR-006 | integration/test_story1_add_and_list.py | `test_add_prints_only_the_identifier` | stdout is exactly `"1\n"`; stderr empty |
+| FR-007 | integration/test_story3_delete.py | `test_ids_increase_and_are_never_reused` | ids 1,2,3; delete 3; next add is 4 (US3 AS3) |
+| FR-008 | unit/test_url_validation.py | `test_only_lowercase_http_https_prefix_accepted` | parametrised accept/reject list; rejected add creates no row and no tag |
+| FR-009 | unit/test_formatting.py | `test_absent_title_defaults_to_empty_string` | stored title is `""`, renders as empty field |
+| FR-010 | unit/test_tag_parsing.py | `test_comma_list_parsed_and_absent_means_no_tags` | `python,cli` → 2 tags; omitted → 0 tags |
+| FR-011 | security/test_security_stdlib_only.py | `test_no_network_or_subprocess_imports` | no `socket`/`subprocess`/`urllib.request` anywhere in shipped source |
+| FR-012 | unit/test_tag_parsing.py | `test_degenerate_tag_inputs` | `""`, `","`, `"a,,b"`, `" a , b "`, `"a,a"` → documented tag sets |
+| FR-013 | integration/test_story1_add_and_list.py | `test_list_prints_all_in_id_order` | US1 AS3 |
+| FR-014 | integration/test_story2_search_and_tag_filter.py | `test_tag_filter_is_exact_and_case_sensitive` | `--tag python` excludes `Python`; matched row shows all its tags (US2 AS2) |
+| FR-015 | integration/test_story2_search_and_tag_filter.py | `test_search_is_case_insensitive_substring` | `PYTHON` matches mixed-case titles and URLs (US2 AS1) |
+| FR-016 | security/test_security_search_literal.py | `test_percent_and_underscore_are_literal` | US2 AS4 |
+| FR-017 | contract/test_output_formats.py | `test_listing_is_four_tab_separated_fields` / `test_tags_sorted_by_code_point` | `line.split("\t")` has length 4; tagless+titleless line ends `\t\t`; `Docs,python` order |
+| FR-018 | contract/test_exit_statuses.py | `test_no_match_prints_nothing_and_exits_zero` | US2 AS3 — stdout and stderr both empty, status 0 |
+| FR-019 | integration/test_story3_delete.py | `test_delete_removes_bookmark_and_its_tags` | row gone; no `bookmark_tags` row for that id (US3 AS1) |
+| FR-020 | integration/test_story3_delete.py | `test_delete_leaves_others_unchanged` | remaining ids, urls, titles, tags byte-identical (US3 AS1) |
