+| FR-025 | integration/test_story4_export.py | `test_special_characters_round_trip` | title with `,`, `"`, `\n`, non-ASCII recovered unchanged via `csv.reader` and `json.loads` (US4 AS3) |
+| FR-026 | security/test_security_args.py | `test_export_format_required_and_restricted` | missing `--format` → 2; `xml`/`CSV`/`""` → 2 |
+| FR-027 | integration/test_story4_export.py | `test_empty_collection_exports` | CSV is header only; JSON is `[]`; status 0 (US4 AS4) |
+
+## Security requirements
+
+Each row names the **negative** case, as Principle V requires.
+
+| Req | Test file | Test function | Negative assertion |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| SR-001 | security/test_security_injection.py | `test_sql_metacharacters_are_literal_text` | add + search `'); DROP TABLE bookmarks;--` as url, title and tag → stored and returned verbatim; `bookmarks` table still exists; all other rows intact |
+| SR-002 | security/test_security_urls.py | `test_url_allowlist_rejects` | parametrised over `javascript:alert(1)`, `file:///etc/passwd`, `data:text/html,x`, `ftp://host/`, `HTTPS://host/`, `example.com`, `//example.com`, `http:/example.com`, `""`, `"   "` → status 2, collection unchanged |
+| SR-003 | security/test_security_args.py | `test_every_malformed_argument_exits_two_without_writing` | malformed `delete` id, bad `--format`, unknown command, unknown option → 2 **and** database file untouched (mtime/size or absent) |
+| SR-004 | security/test_security_search_literal.py | `test_search_for_percent_does_not_match_row_without_percent` | searching `%` returns no rows when no title/url contains a literal `%` |
+| SR-005 | security/test_security_file_mode.py | `test_file_mode_is_0600` | `stat().st_mode & 0o777 == 0o600` after first use; POSIX-only guard; also asserts mode is correct immediately after creation, not re-chmodded |
+| SR-006 | security/test_security_limits.py | `test_one_char_over_each_limit_is_rejected` | URL 8193, title 4097, `--tags` 4097 chars, 65 tags, tag 129 chars, search 1025 → status 2 and nothing stored; boundary-exact values (8192/4096/64/128/1024) accepted |
+| SR-007 | security/test_security_streaming.py | `test_export_of_50k_bookmarks_is_memory_bounded` | seed 50,000 rows; export under `tracemalloc` peak below a fixed ceiling independent of collection size; compare peak at 5k vs 50k to show no proportional growth |
+| SR-008 | security/test_security_no_traceback.py | `test_expected_failures_are_single_line_and_disclose_nothing` | for each of invalid URL, missing id, bad argument, unusable database: stderr is one line, contains no `Traceback`, no `sqlite3`, no `SELECT`/`INSERT`/`DELETE` |
+| SR-009 | security/test_security_atomicity.py | `test_failed_add_leaves_no_partial_row_or_orphan_tag` | an `add` that fails validation, and an `add` whose tag insert raises mid-transaction (monkeypatched), leave zero `bookmarks` rows and zero `bookmark_tags` rows; `delete` of a missing id commits nothing |
+| SR-010 | security/test_security_stdlib_only.py | `test_no_shell_subprocess_socket_or_env_config` | AST walk of `src/bookmarks/**.py`: every imported top-level module in `sys.stdlib_module_names`; `subprocess`, `socket`, `os.system`, `os.popen`, `os.environ` absent |
+| SR-011 | security/test_security_no_residual_files.py | `test_no_temp_or_journal_files_remain` | after each of the five commands (and after a failing one), the db directory contains exactly the database file — no `-journal`, `-wal`, `-shm` or temp file |
+
